window.docContents[191].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.CryptoGames.DH.X25519Group/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___CryptoGames___DH___X25519Group":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications/CryptoGames/DH › X25519Group.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 63 of 123 lines trusted trust banner B2, trusted: definitions used by the statement source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (15)def twistOrderLdef x25519ZeroKeydef x25519BaseKeydef isX25519SubgroupKeydef X25519Ptinstance L73instance L76def publicKeyFintypeinstance L87def x25519BasePtdef x25519Dhdef x25519EncTdef x25519EncPtdef x25519DecTdef x25519Delta\n\nConcrete X25519 Prime-Order Subgroup SpecificationTrusted: definitions used by the statement. Defines the concrete Curve25519 prime-order x-only subgroup X25519Pt, its RFC 7748 Diffie–Hellman action x25519Dh, wire encoding/decoding (x25519EncPt, x25519EncT, x25519DecT), uniform subgroup sampler (SampleableType X25519Pt), and clamped base-point fiber bound x25519Delta = 1 / 2 ^ 250. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Elements of X25519Pt are canonical 32-byte little-endian Montgomery u-coordinates: 0^32 (the identity) together with the (edOrderL - 1) / 2 canonical prime-order points satisfying u < p25519, montLiftEd u 0 = some P, and [edOrderL] P = edZero. Wire decoding x25519DecT is the polynomial-time canonical subgroup membership test; x25519Dh is RFC 7748 x25519Ref restricted to X25519Pt (the fallback else 0 branch is provably unreachable).\n\n\n\ndef twistOrderLL45–48 ↗#Prime subgroup order ℓ' of the Curve25519 quadratic twist E'(𝔽_p), satisfying |E'(𝔽_p)| = 4 * ℓ' and 8 * edOrderL + 4 * twistOrderL = 2 * (p25519 + 1).\n\ndef x25519ZeroKeyL50–52 ↗#All-zero 32-byte encoding representing the identity element of X25519Pt.\n\ndef x25519BaseKeyL54–56 ↗#Standard Curve25519 Montgomery basepoint u = 9 as a PublicKey.\n\ndef isX25519SubgroupKeyL58–66 ↗#Decidable membership predicate for the Curve25519 prime-order x-only subgroup: either 0^32 (the identity) or a canonical Montgomery u-coordinate < p25519 whose even-x Edwards lift lies in the edOrderL-torsion subgroup.\n\ndef X25519PtL68–71 ↗#Prime-order x-only subgroup of Curve25519, represented by canonical 32-byte Montgomery u-coordinates (0^32 together with the (edOrderL - 1) / 2 canonical prime-order points).\n\ninstanceL73–74 ↗#\n\ninstanceL76–77 ↗#\n\ndef publicKeyFintypeL79–85 ↗#Finite enumeration structure on PublicKey via its underlying 32-byte vector.\n\ninstanceL87–91 ↗#Canonical uniform sampler over X25519Pt (uniform measure on all (edOrderL + 1) / 2 canonical subgroup elements).\n\ndef x25519BasePtL93–96 ↗#Curve25519 Montgomery basepoint u = 9 in X25519Pt. The else 0 branch is provably unreachable.\n\ndef x25519DhL98–104 ↗#Concrete RFC 7748 X25519 Diffie–Hellman action on X25519Pt. The else 0 branch is provably unreachable because RFC 7748 clamped scalar multiplication preserves X25519Pt.\n\ndef x25519EncTL106–108 ↗#32-byte wire encoding of Q : X25519Pt as a PublicKey.\n\ndef x25519EncPtL110–112 ↗#32-byte little-endian Montgomery encoding of Q : X25519Pt.\n\ndef x25519DecTL114–116 ↗#Polynomial-time canonical prime-order subgroup decoder PublicKey → Option X25519Pt.\n\ndef x25519DeltaL118–121 ↗#Tight clamped X25519 base-point fiber probability bound 2^-250: each point has at most 2 signs mod edOrderL times 2^5 clamped-away bits (64 / 2^256 = 1 / 2^250).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/CryptoGames/DH/X25519Group.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.CryptoGames.DH.X25519Group/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___CryptoGames___DH___X25519Group"}});